audit history
```

---

# 116. HOLIDAY TESTS

Test:

```text
organization holiday
branch holiday
optional holiday
duplicate holiday
holiday assignment
leave excluding holiday
```

---

# 117. ATTENDANCE INTEGRATION TESTS

Test:

```text
Approved leave → ON_LEAVE
Half-day leave + attendance
Holiday + attendance
Weekly off + attendance
Leave cancellation → balance reversal
Regularization approval → attendance update
```

---

# 118. CONCURRENCY TESTS

Important cases:

```text
Two leave approvals
Two leave requests consuming same balance
Leave approval + cancellation
Accrual job retry
Approval action retry
```

---

# 119. TENANT SECURITY TESTS

Explicitly test:

```text
Tenant A cannot see Tenant B leave.
Tenant A cannot see Tenant B balance.
Tenant A cannot modify Tenant B holiday.
Tenant A cannot approve Tenant B request.
Tenant A cannot modify Tenant B regularization.
Tenant A cannot access Tenant B workflow.
```

---

# 120. DATABASE TESTS

Verify:

```text
Foreign keys
Unique constraints
Date constraints
Tenant constraints
Leave ledger integrity
Approval relationships
Transaction rollback
```

---

# 121. PROPERTY / EDGE CASE TESTING

Test:

```text
Leap year
Month boundary
Year boundary
Leave-year boundary
Holiday on weekly off
Multiple holidays
Half-day
Zero duration
Negative duration
Start date > end date
Same-day leave
Backdated leave
Future leave
Employee joins mid-year
Employee leaves mid-year
Inactive employee
Terminated employee
```

---

# 122. PERFORMANCE TESTING

Use realistic datasets:

```text
10,000 employees
5+ leave types
Several years of leave ledger
Thousands of leave requests
Thousands of approval actions
Large holiday calendars
```

Test:

```text
Employee balance
Leave history
Manager approval inbox
HR dashboard
Calendar
```

Avoid N+1 queries.

---

# 123. LEAVE LEDGER PERFORMANCE

Do not calculate balances by scanning millions of ledger records for every request.

Use appropriate:

```text
Indexes
Materialized/current balance
Aggregations
Caching where safe
```

But preserve ledger as the audit source of balance changes.

---

# 124. ACCRUAL JOB PERFORMANCE

Accrual jobs must process tenants/employees efficiently.

Avoid:

```text
One database query per employee
```

Use batching/bulk operations where safe.

---

# 125. JOB FAILURE HANDLING

Background jobs must support:

```text
Retry
Idempotency
Logging
Failure reporting
Partial failure handling
```

Do not grant duplicate leave because a job was retried.

---

# 126. OBSERVABILITY

Add metrics/logging for:

```text
leave.request.created
leave.request.approved
leave.request.rejected
leave.request.cancelled
leave.balance.adjusted
leave.accrual.completed
leave.accrual.failed
approval.completed
approval.rejected
regularization.created
regularization.approved
regularization.rejected
```

Do not log sensitive employee information unnecessarily.

---

# 127. AUDIT RETENTION

Keep important approval and balance history.

Do not physically delete:

```text
approval actions
leave ledger transactions
regularization history
```

through normal CRUD operations.

---

# 128. DATA PRIVACY

Do not expose:

```text
medical documents
private reasons
attachments
personal information
```

to users without authorization.

Managers may need limited information while HR may have broader permissions.

Use least privilege.

---

# 129. API DOCUMENTATION

All endpoints must have:

```text
Summary
Description
Request schema
Response schema
Authentication
Authorization
Validation errors
Business errors
```

Ensure OpenAPI is accurate.

---

# 130. MIGRATIONS

Create proper PostgreSQL migrations.

Test:

```text
Fresh database
Existing Phase 1–5 database
Migration upgrade
Rollback where supported
```

Do not manually edit production schema.

---

# 131. SEED DATA

For development, create safe demo data:

```text
Leave Types
Leave Policies
Holiday Calendar
Holidays
Approval Workflow
Sample balances
```

Never add real employee information.

---

# 132. BACKWARD COMPATIBILITY

Phase 6 must not break:

```text
Phase 1
Phase 2
Phase 3
Phase 4
Phase 5
```

